{
  "name": "HVAC Missed Call Recovery Engine — Instant Text-Back + Intent Routing + No-Reply Escalation",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## \ud83d\udd25 HVAC Missed Call Recovery Engine\n\n**What this does, end to end:**\n1. Twilio tells us the instant a call ends. We detect if it was missed (no-answer, busy, voicemail, or hang-up before pickup).\n2. Within seconds we upsert the caller in GoHighLevel and text them back with a message that changes tone depending on business hours vs after-hours/emergency.\n3. We log every miss and ping the owner on Slack so nothing is invisible.\n4. If they reply, a second webhook parses their intent (emergency / repair / install / maintenance) and routes them: emergencies get an URGENT owner alert (and optionally an immediate outbound AI voice call), everyone else gets a booking link.\n5. If they DON'T reply within 20 minutes, we send one follow-up text and tell the owner to call manually \u2014 nobody falls through the cracks silently.\n\n**Setup checklist:**\n1. Twilio: on your HVAC number, set the Voice \u2192 Call Status Changes webhook to the Branch 1 webhook's production URL, method POST, and check 'completed', 'no-answer', 'busy', 'failed'.\n2. GoHighLevel: create a Private Integration token (Settings \u2192 Private Integrations) with scopes contacts.readonly, contacts.write, conversations.readonly, conversations.write, conversations/message.write. Use it as an HTTP Header Auth credential: header 'Authorization' = 'Bearer YOUR_TOKEN', and every GHL call also needs a 'Version' header (check GoHighLevel's current API docs for the latest date string \u2014 this changes).\n3. Point GoHighLevel's inbound SMS/conversation webhook (or Twilio's inbound message webhook, whichever you're using for replies) at the Branch 2 webhook's production URL.\n4. Replace every YOUR_* placeholder: locationId, owner phone/Slack channel, business hours, Vapi assistant ID if you wire in the emergency outbound call.\n5. GHL's exact contact-search and message endpoints shift between API versions \u2014 verify the two HTTP Request nodes marked \u26a0\ufe0f against GoHighLevel's current API v2 docs before going live.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "note_main",
      "name": "README",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-2000, -200]
    },

    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "hvac-missed-call",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "wh_call_status",
      "name": "Twilio Call Status Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [-1360, 0],
      "webhookId": "hvac-missed-call"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Twilio posts form-encoded fields on every call status change.\nconst b = $input.first().json.body || $input.first().json;\n\nconst callStatus = (b.CallStatus || '').toLowerCase();\nconst duration = parseInt(b.CallDuration || b.DialCallDuration || '0', 10);\nconst from = b.From || b.Caller || '';\nconst to = b.To || b.Called || '';\nconst callSid = b.CallSid || '';\nconst direction = b.Direction || 'inbound';\n\n// Missed = never answered, OR answered-and-hung-up in under 4s (rang once, hung up before pickup / voicemail beep).\nconst neverAnswered = ['no-answer', 'busy', 'failed'].includes(callStatus);\nconst bailedEarly = callStatus === 'completed' && duration > 0 && duration <= 4;\nconst isMissed = (neverAnswered || bailedEarly) && direction === 'inbound';\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    isMissed,\n    callStatus,\n    duration,\n    callerPhone: from,\n    businessPhone: to,\n    callSid,\n    receivedAt: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "code_normalize_call",
      "name": "Normalize Call Event",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [-1160, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": { "version": 2 },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.isMissed }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": { "type": "boolean", "operation": "true" }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        }
      },
      "id": "if_missed",
      "name": "Is Missed Call?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [-960, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "text",
        "responseBody": "OK",
        "options": { "responseCode": 200 }
      },
      "id": "respond_ignore",
      "name": "Ack — Call Was Answered",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [-760, 180]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Decide tone + whether to flag this as an emergency-hours miss.\n// Business hours: Mon-Sat 8am-6pm local. Adjust to the shop's real hours.\nconst now = new Date();\nconst day = now.getDay(); // 0 = Sun\nconst hour = now.getHours();\n\nconst isBusinessHours = day >= 1 && day <= 6 && hour >= 8 && hour < 18;\n\nconst ownerName = 'YOUR_OWNER_NAME';\nconst businessName = 'YOUR_HVAC_COMPANY';\n\nconst message = isBusinessHours\n  ? `Hey, sorry we missed you! This is ${ownerName} from ${businessName}. Are you calling about AC repair, heating repair, installation, or maintenance? Reply and I'll get you sorted right away.`\n  : `Thanks for calling ${businessName}! We're closed right now but if this is a no-heat, no-cool, or leak emergency, reply EMERGENCY and we'll call you back immediately. Otherwise let us know what you need and we'll follow up first thing.`;\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...$json,\n    isBusinessHours,\n    initialMessage: message,\n    ownerName,\n    businessName\n  }\n}];"
      },
